# Nexus contract (v2.2.0)

Plugin `2.2.0` (Cursor, Claude Code, Codex). Follow `$using-nexus` (session bootstrap where hooks exist). Procedures live in skills — do not invent workflows.

## Loop

1. Preferences — read `.nexus/user/preferences.md` when present.
2. Workspace — `$git-assistant` → `workspace-choice` before first edit (`main` | named worktree).
3. Act — smallest change; `$architect` before new files/modules.
4. Style — `$code-style` on touched files.
5. Review — `$integrity-review` on the affected area.
6. Closeout — on Clean/Corrected: `$git-assistant` → `closeout`; on Uncertain: stop.

## Routing

| Task | Skill |
| --- | --- |
| Bootstrap / skill discipline | `$using-nexus` |
| Git, workspace, closeout | `$git-assistant` |
| Final review | `$integrity-review` |
| Structure / placement | `$architect` |
| Style | `$code-style` |
| React | `$frontend` |
| README | `$readme-writer` |
| Logs | `$log-writer` |
| Memory | `$memory` |
| Browser | `$playwright` |

## Hard gates

- No worktree, commit, merge to `main`, or push without approval for that step.
- Superpowers docs (`docs/superpowers/`, `.superpowers/`): preference `commit superpowers docs` = `include` | `exclude` | `ask` (default ask).
- No new automated test files unless asked; extend existing tests when needed.
- English for code/commits/harness docs; UI copy follows product language only when requested.
- Prefer uv for Python when the repo uses it; else local convention.
- Naming: single-word files/modules preferred (two max); public before private; normalize only files you touch.
- If Superpowers is also loaded: Nexus wins for workspace, closeout, and test policy.

## Memory

`.nexus/user/` preferences and `.nexus/project/` learnings are local to the app repo. Write only via `$memory` on explicit request. No secrets.
